#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Streaming data\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "One of the core primitives of the AT Protocol is the *firehose*. It is an authenticated stream of events used to efficiently sync user updates (posts, likes, follows, handle changes, etc).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many AT applications that need to stream incoming data will utilize the firehose — from feed generators to labelers, to bots and search engines. In the AT ecosystem, there are many different endpoints that seed these firehose APIs. Each PDS serves a stream of all of the activity on the repos it is responsible for. From there, Relays aggregate the streams of each participating PDS into a single unified stream — the firehose.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Firehose\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anyone can connect to the firehose without authentication — this is a core feature of the protocol. To get started, open a WebSocket connection to any provider of the `com.atproto.sync.subscribeRepos` endpoint:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```shell \n"
"$ websocat wss://bsky.network/xrpc/com.atproto.sync.subscribeRepos\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "From here, you would need to read each message as it comes in, and decode the associated data. Our [Go](https://github.com/bluesky-social/indigo) SDK is currently the most feature-complete for interacting with the firehose directly.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bear in mind that firehose output format is one of the more complex parts of AT, involving decoding binary [CBOR](/specs/data-model) data and [CAR](/specs/repository#car-file-serialization) files. Additionally, the volume of data has increased rapidly as the network has grown. The full synchronization firehose is core network infrastructure, but for end users such as [feed developers](/guides/feeds), we provide an alternative streaming solution called **Jetstream.**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Jetstream\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Jetstream has a few key advantages:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- simple JSON encoding\n"
"- reduced bandwidth, and compression\n"
"- ability to filter by collection (NSID) or repo (DID)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Jetstream server consumes from the firehose and fans out to many subscribers. It is [open source](https://github.com/bluesky-social/jetstream), implemented in Go, simple to self-host. There is an official client library included (in Go), and [community client libraries](https://skyware.js.org/guides/jetstream/introduction/getting-started/) have been developed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can work with Jetstream like any other websocket. Just provide a Jetstream endpoint like `wss://jetstream2.us-east.bsky.network/subscribe`, and a `wantedCollections` parameter, like `?wantedCollections=app.bsky.feed.post`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a Python example:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:41
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```python\n"
"import asyncio\n"
"import websockets\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "uri = \"wss://jetstream2.us-east.bsky.network/subscribe?wantedCollections=app.bsky.feed.post\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:55
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"async def listen_to_websocket():\n"
"  async with websockets.connect(uri) as websocket:\n"
"    while True:\n"
"      try:\n"
"        message = await websocket.recv()\n"
"        print(message)\n"
"      except websockets.ConnectionClosed as e:\n"
"        print(f\"Connection closed: {e}\")\n"
"        break\n"
"      except Exception as e:\n"
"        print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/streaming-data/en.mdx:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"asyncio.get_event_loop().run_until_complete(listen_to_websocket())\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

